  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reaching out. Your account is active and VPN access is turned on, but Duo has not been set up for your account yet. That's why the VPN asks for a Duo approval you can't complete. This is normal for a laptop issued without Duo. To finish setup, we need a short session (remote or in person) with your phone with you. Please install the Duo Mobile app from your app store before the session. Reply with a few times that work for you this week and we'll set it up. Also, your account is flagged to change your password at your next sign-in, so you may be asked to choose a new one when you first log in. We'll confirm the details with you when we talk.",
  "internal_note": "Checked: lookup_user shows account active, vpn_access true, sign_in_blocked false, failed_login_count 0, must_change_password true, password last set 2026-10-11. check_mfa_status shows enrolled:false, so Duo was never enrolled (matches KB-004 'not enrolled' case). Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Win 11, assigned to Hannah) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:57 UTC, 130 GB free, no warnings. Next step per KB-004: schedule a remote or in-person enrollment session with Hannah present with her phone. Check the Duo client is installed on the laptop during the session, then enroll via activation QR and send a test push. No sign-in lockout or block. I have no scheduling tool, so a technician needs to book the session. Not a security concern (no unexpected pushes reported). Confirm the laptop's Duo client during the session.",
